  "foaf:name": "Biodiversity of the Blue Ocean cluster (BBO)",
  "sdo:name": "Biodiversity of the Blue Ocean cluster (BBO)",
  "sdo:description": "In the four projects within the Biodiversity of the Blue Ocean cluster, 65 researchers are developing novel approaches to better understand the complex interactions in ocean ecosystems and make the best possible predictions of future biodiversity. This knowledge supports efforts to protect marine biodiversity within the framework of the Agreement under the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction. Each project has its own research focus, ranging from mapping benthic ecosystems in the Weddell Sea, designing decision-making tools for the planning of marine protected areas, developing novel biodiversity indicators and building past-informed models to predict the future of marine ecosystems. The projects work closely with (inter)national stakeholders in the co-design, co-production and co-evaluation of knowledge to ensure that the research results are transferred into practice.",
  "sdo:location": "Germany",
  "sdo:identifier": "49.1",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/biodiversity-of-the-blue-ocean-cluster-bbo/",
